   "daf": "35b",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "נִקְלַף. אָמַר רָבָא: הַאי אֶתְרוֹגָא דְּאַגְלֵיד כַּאֲהִינָא סוּמָּקָא — כְּשֵׁרָה. וְהָא אֲנַן תְּנַן: נִקְלַף — פָּסוּל! לָא קַשְׁיָא,",
   "en": "The mishna continues: An etrog that «was peeled» is unfit. «Rava said: This etrog that was peeled like a red date» so that only its thin, outer peel is removed but the rest remains intact, «is fit.» The Gemara objects: «But didn’t we learn» explicitly in the mishna: If the etrog «was peeled» it is unfit? The Gemara answers: This is «not difficult;»"
  }
 ],
